this video is going to be sponsored by  books but more on them later so i think  if you're starting the new year after  summers and you're a student you're  probably wondering what kind of products  you need or what kind of tools you could  use such that you can optimize your  studying so i'm here to help you to show  you the products that i've used over the  last few years during my bachelor's  master's and now my phd i have really  for me optimized and increased my  studying productivity so let's get  straight into it so the first product i  want to talk about are noise cancelling  headphones and i have two of them and  that's just because one of them broke  down a while ago but then it suddenly  started doing it again and i was really  surprised about that so the first one i  bought almost five years ago i think are  these bose headphones and if you're  wondering what you should buy bose or  sony i think they're actually really  similar bose and sony um but i have to  say noise cancelling headphones for me  have been maybe one of the products i  love the most aside from my laptop of  course and that's because i study in a  lot of environments i've studied in  airplanes i've studied in trains i had  to study in busy cafes i also have  roommates and roommates of course that  talk a lot or whatever and i think  having these you can kind of study in  any environment and if you're a student  and you don't have any money i was also  in that predicament a few a while ago so  then i just used earplugs of course and  i think they're very similar but i also  love listening to music so i now have  these the sony so i upgraded from the  bose to the sony but to be honest  they're almost the same so i would just  try to buy the cheapest ones or try to  find the cheapest ones but noise  cancelling headphones have been such  lifesavers so yeah if you're  studying in a really loud environment or  you have family that's talking all the  time i would really consider buying one  of these um they have saved my life in  many situations so the next tool i want  to talk about is of course if you watch  this channel for a while is notion and i  personally love notion i think it's a  tool that i have used the most so  throughout my channel i've talked a lot  about notion but i use it for almost  anything so i use it to keep my class  notes i use it when i'm myself teaching  so i was a ta for example at nurmage a  little while ago and i made this page  such that i could remember all the notes  students had to take or which class  schedule was where and i also personally  love it for learning new skills so i'm  usually also randomly learning new  skills so something i'm working on at  the moment is to create a website and i  on this website i have many ideas what i  want to do but the first thing usually  what i start when i want to make  something new is i do this deep dive or  this research into websites i love for  example or how i want my website to look  like and i usually put all of that in  notion and notion for me then becomes  almost this research bank with  everything from topics i love in my life  but also topics that i learned at school  and i think if you're a student it's  really important to have a bank like  this that you can put all your ideas in  because as a student you will go through  life learning many things and you will  also forget many things but it's so nice  if you can look up topics that you used  to be interested in or that you're  interested in in the future and then you  can just put it all in one place and  re-remember some of the things you learn  so the next thing i really think every  student should have is an e-reader so i  have this e-reader it's a kobo and i  bought this because it's pretty cheap  and i use this almost daily so i always  have this in my bag so whenever i have a  moment between um traveling or i'm bored  at a certain point i usually grab my  e-reader and i start reading i also read  a lot on my phone and on my ipad and the  amounts of books i go through on my  e-reader are a lot so i love to buy hard  copies and soft copies as well but  sometimes i'm not really sure if i would  like a book and then i think it's a  little bit wasteful if i have all these  books lying around that i don't really  enjoy so if i'm not sure about a book i  usually first have it on my e-reader and  i think a really good challenge to take  if you have an e-reader is to try to  replace most of your phone time by  e-reading time i think if you try to do  this throughout the week you will really  see how much you actually use your phone  and if you replace this by an e-reader  how much more you read so i sometimes do  this when i notice that i'm on my phone  too much i try to challenge myself to  replace that time by using my e-reader  which brings me to today's sponsor books  they were kind enough to send me one of  their products which is the note air 2  plus so i really like this note because  it's kind of between an ipad and an  e-reader in the fact that it's still  kind for your eyes so it doesn't have a  bright screen like an ipad but you can  write on it like an ipad which i really  love so i used to read most of my papers  for example on my ipad and i also read a  lot of ebooks on my ipad because i  really love writing on the things that  i'm learning about i think if you write  whilst you're learning you actually  retain more of the information so i  usually when i read a really difficult  book for school for example i usually  put little notes or little question  marks in the margin and the thing is  although i love the ipad it is really a  screen and i think my screen time at the  moment is about 10 hours so that's what  i really like about this product because  it's still really good for your eyes and  it doesn't strain your eyes because it's  very similar to a book so right now i'm  reading a few books on this i'm reading  think like a monk i think it's really  interesting i would highly recommend it  i'm reading the comfort but book by matt  hay um this one is a bit dubious i'm not  sure if i like it too much the one thing  i do like about it is that there are a  lot of quotes in it and then i can write  little inspirational messages to myself  and the last book i'm reading is  earthlings by sayaka muhata and that  book is strange that's the only thing i  can say about that book but if you love  reading and you're also a student i do  think this is a really nice product to  have in your kit and to consider as an  alternative for the ipad so the next  tool i use a lot of which i have also  talked about is pomodoro timer so there  are a few pomodoro timers i really love  i love forest of course just because  it's super aesthetic and i kind of like  to have it on my computer for example  and just show this really aesthetically  pleasing screen but i also use promo  focus dot io and this is just it's less  aesthetically pleasing but it's free and  i find the interface a little bit more  intuitive so i usually use two types of  cycles of pomodoros or i use 25 minutes  and then five minutes rest and these are  usually for things tasks i'm really  putting off so when i have these 25  minutes i just that's just kind of to  put me into flow or to really push me to  finish something and i also use these 15  minutes 10 minutes rest and that's  usually for longer projects but i  personally really love pomodoros i don't  always use it i've talked about this  before but i think if you are doing a  little bit more flow work where you're  really getting into this flow and deep  work i think then pomodoros are not  really suitable for that i would just  try to keep on working until you get  really tired but i think if you for  example really have to cram for an exam  using pomodoros can really motivate you  and also can keep you on the task  because you're not really allowed to use  twitter for example or facebook in  between and that really allows you to  focus your mind so to say and the last  thing i want to talk about number five  is just to have a planner slash notebook  so i always carry a notebook with me  even though i have now my note air and i  have an ipad and all these electronical  devices because throughout the day i  think you get a lot of good ideas and  it's good to scribble them down  somewhere because otherwise you forget  them and of course i also record them in  the phone but some of these thoughts  require a little bit more thought or a  little bit more deep diving and then i  think it's good to just take a minute  and to really write down what you're  thinking about also something i love to  do is journal and i don't journal  consistently but i do try every day at  the end of the day or at the beginning  of the day to write three things down  that i loved about the day or that i'm  looking forward to and i think that just  kind of gives a positive mindset or a  positive way to think about your day and  i really learned this from my friend  sage um because she's been doing this  consistently for years and she does it  on her github which i think is really  cool but seeing the things she writes  down and looking back through her notes  is just really fun and it really shows a  really fun life that she's actually  having and all the experiences she's  having with her friends and her dog  charlie and that's just for me really  fun to see and i think another way i use  it is i also have this thicker planner  which i bought online somewhere for  really cheap but the thing i really love  about this planner is it has these  hour blocks and i sometimes love to  write down just a rough plan of what i'm  thinking of doing throughout the day and  i don't always do this i don't always  think it's necessary sometimes i just  want to accomplish one or two things  that i really have to focus on  throughout the day but especially if my  days are a little bit more busy i like  to plan them out such that i don't feel  as overwhelmed so these are tools i've  always used during my studying an  e-reader and laptop and my headphones  and then i'm good to go wherever i am  and i don't think you really need  anything else and if you have a product  or tool that you really love and use a  90 of your studying time i would love to  hear about it please put it down in the  comments below because i would always  like to optimize my studying and my  studying routine and otherwise i'll see  you next week bye

